window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b268-599d47e7adf2fb9a.json"]={sha256:"599d47e7adf2fb9aa301c6c26fd981fbeab3274f0e24f76bb244e23e1f2ba62a",value:{"id":"b268","title":"河岸取水口防淤設計","titleEn":"Sediment-resistant river intake design","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"課程由季節分流和泥砂輸入開始，逐步分析沉降、沉砂面積、起動剪應力、篩網方向與沖砂水量，再以庫容和縮尺試驗建立可驗證的維護策略。紅崖與弗里波特提供真實取水工程背景，所有量值為獨立教學假設，不把水理比較當成魚類保護、許可或現場操作判定。","summaryEn":"Starting with seasonal diversion and sediment input, the course develops settling, basin area, incipient-motion stress, screen orientation and flushing-volume analyses, then connects storage and scale experiments to verifiable maintenance planning. Red Bluff and Freeport provide real intake context. Numerical values are independent assumptions, and hydraulic comparisons do not establish fish protection, permission or field operating decisions.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-rivers","subcategoryTitle":"輸配水、河川與都市防洪","subcategoryTitleEn":"Water conveyance, rivers and urban flood protection","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-rivers","learningTags":["water","water-rivers","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-pipe","architectureNodes":[["河川工況","River states"],["泥砂輸入","Sediment input"],["取水篩網","Intake screen"],["沖砂與庫容","Flushing and storage"],["現地驗證","Field verification"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4]],"diagram":{"type":"water-pipe","labels":["河川工況","泥砂輸入","取水篩網","沖砂與庫容","現地驗證"],"labelsEn":["River states","Sediment input","Intake screen","Flushing and storage","Field verification"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"敏感度以稀薄、不絮凝球形顆粒的斯托克斯模型為基準，水黏度0.001 Pa·s、顆粒及水密度2650與1000 kg/m³。粒徑由20 μm增至22 μm，只增加10%，沉降速度卻由0.0003597增至0.0004352 m/s，增加21%；顆粒雷諾數由0.00719增至0.00958，仍符合此理想低雷諾數比較。這不能代表絮凝泥或實際沉砂率，因為粒徑分布、短路和再懸浮未納入。若改變粒徑到粗砂，必須重新檢查阻力流態，而不是繼續使用平方比例。","textEn":"Use the Stokes model for dilute, nonflocculating spheres with viscosity 0.001 Pa·s and particle/water densities 2650 and 1000 kg/m³. Increasing diameter from 20 to 22 μm is only a ten-percent change, but settling speed increases from 0.0003597 to 0.0004352 m/s, or 21%. Particle Reynolds number rises from 0.00719 to 0.00958, remaining small for this ideal comparison. This is not a prediction of flocculating mud or actual basin removal, because size distributions, short-circuiting and resuspension are excluded. Moving to coarse sand requires a fresh drag-regime check rather than continued use of the squared-diameter scaling.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b268-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「引水比例與季節工況機理與驗證」與「懸移質輸入帳機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Diversion fraction and seasonal states mechanism and verification\" and \"Suspended-sediment input budget mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b268-v15-01","title":"引水比例與季節工況機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Diversion fraction and seasonal states mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「引水比例與季節工況」如何影響河岸取水口防淤設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Diversion fraction and seasonal states” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sediment-resistant river intake design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"河岸取水會改變局部分流與近岸流線，防淤設計必須同時考慮供水、河川剩餘流量與魚類通行。洪水期高含砂不一定和最大取水量同時發生，枯水期則可能暴露取水門檻或降低掃流。單一設計流量會掩蓋季節差異，應用成組水位、流量和泥砂資料描述實際可能的工況。本例只是整體水量分配，沒有推導局部流線或可容許取水比例；下游需求與許可條件須另由實際資料確認。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「引水比例與季節工況」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A river intake alters local flow division and near-bank streamlines, linking sediment management to supply, remaining river flow and fish passage. High flood sediment does not necessarily coincide with maximum diversion, while low water may expose the sill or weaken sweeping flow. One design discharge hides seasonal differences; paired stage, flow and sediment records should define physically plausible operating states. The example is a bulk flow allocation, not a prediction of local streamlines or an allowable diversion fraction. Downstream requirements and permission conditions need separate evidence. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Diversion fraction and seasonal states” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設河流Qr=80 m³/s、取水Qd=8 m³/s，引水比r=Qd/Qr=0.10，忽略其他支流後剩餘72 m³/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume river Qr=80 m³/s and diversion Qd=8 m³/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要取水量低於年平均河川流量，就不必分析枯水分流。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Diversion below annual mean river flow makes low-flow allocation analysis unnecessary.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「引水比例與季節工況」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Diversion fraction and seasonal states”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-01-k1","title":"引水比例與季節工況機理與驗證","titleEn":"Diversion fraction and seasonal states mechanism and verification","text":"河岸取水會改變局部分流與近岸流線，防淤設計必須同時考慮供水、河川剩餘流量與魚類通行。洪水期高含砂不一定和最大取水量同時發生，枯水期則可能暴露取水門檻或降低掃流。","textEn":"A river intake alters local flow division and near-bank streamlines, linking sediment management to supply, remaining river flow and fish passage. High flood sediment does not necessarily coincide with maximum diversion, while low water may expose the sill or weaken sweeping flow.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要取水量低於年平均河川流量，就不必分析枯水分流。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Diversion below annual mean river flow makes low-flow allocation analysis unnecessary. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「引水比例與季節工況機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Diversion fraction and seasonal states mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["只要取水量低於年平均河川流量，就不必分析枯水分流。","河岸取水會改變局部分流與近岸流線，防淤設計必須同時考慮供水、河川剩餘流量與魚類通行。","取水流量固定時，只量一次濁度就能確定整場泥砂輸入。"],"optionsEn":["Diversion below annual mean river flow makes low-flow allocation analysis unnecessary.","A river intake alters local flow division and near-bank streamlines, linking sediment management to supply, remaining river flow and fish passage.","With constant diversion, one turbidity measurement determines the entire event sediment input."],"answer":1,"explanation":"河岸取水會改變局部分流與近岸流線，防淤設計必須同時考慮供水、河川剩餘流量與魚類通行。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A river intake alters local flow division and near-bank streamlines, linking sediment management to supply, remaining river flow and fish passage. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b268-v15-02","title":"引水比例與季節工況機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Diversion fraction and seasonal states mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「引水比例與季節工況」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Diversion fraction and seasonal states” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設河流Qr=80 m³/s、取水Qd=8 m³/s，引水比r=Qd/Qr=0.10，忽略其他支流後剩餘72 m³/s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume river Qr=80 m³/s and diversion Qd=8 m³/s. Fraction r=Qd/Qr=0.10, leaving 72 m³/s when other streams are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將取水紀錄與同時河川流量配對，分別整理枯水、常水及洪水事件。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Pair diversion records with simultaneous river flow and separate low, ordinary and flood events.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設河流Qr=80 m³/s、取水Qd=8 m³/s，引水比r=Qd/Qr=0.10，忽略其他支流後剩餘72 m³/s。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume river Qr=80 m³/s and diversion Qd=8 m³/s. Fraction r=Qd/Qr=0.10, leaving 72 m³/s when other streams are excluded.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「引水比例與季節工況機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Diversion fraction and seasonal states mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["沉砂池只要越深，所有粒徑的理想去除效率就一定越高。","均勻流平均剪應力就是每個角落與閘門下方的真實床面應力。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設河流Qr=80 m³/s、取水Qd=8 m³/s，引水比r=Qd/Qr=0.10，忽略其他支流後剩餘72 m³/s。"],"optionsEn":["A deeper settling basin necessarily improves ideal removal for every grain size.","Uniform-flow mean shear equals actual bed stress in every corner and beneath every gate.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume river Qr=80 m³/s and diversion Qd=8 m³/s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設河流Qr=80 m³/s、取水Qd=8 m³/s，引水比r=Qd/Qr=0.10，忽略其他支流後剩餘72 m³/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume river Qr=80 m³/s and diversion Qd=8 m³/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b268-v15-03","title":"引水比例與季節工況機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Diversion fraction and seasonal states mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「引水比例與季節工況」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Diversion fraction and seasonal states” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將取水紀錄與同時河川流量配對，分別整理枯水、常水及洪水事件。核對上游支流與下游量測的控制體，避免用不同時刻的流量計算分流比，再驗證門檻高程是否仍淹沒。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Pair diversion records with simultaneous river flow and separate low, ordinary and flood events. Check tributaries and downstream measurement control volumes, avoiding ratios formed from different times, then verify whether the intake sill remains submerged in each selected state. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：製作三種季節工況表，為每列填入同時水位、流量與濃度。將資料缺口列出，說明哪種缺測會妨礙判斷淹沒、泥砂或魚類掃流條件。","observationEn":"Site practice: Create three seasonal scenarios with simultaneous stage, discharge and concentration. Identify missing observations and explain which gaps prevent assessment of submergence, sediment behavior or fish-guiding sweeping flow.","failure":"注意干擾：用年平均流量判斷取水比例會掩蓋枯水壓力，將洪水流量和低水位拼接則可能形成不可能工況；未檢查剩餘流量也會把防淤效率與河川功能割裂。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An annual mean conceals low-flow pressure, while combining flood discharge with unrelated low stage may create an impossible scenario. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將取水紀錄與同時河川流量配對，分別整理枯水、常水及洪水事件。核對上游支流與下游量測的控制體，避免用不同時刻的流量計算分流比，再驗證門檻高程是否仍淹沒。","textEn":"Pair diversion records with simultaneous river flow and separate low, ordinary and flood events. Check tributaries and downstream measurement control volumes, avoiding ratios formed from different times, then verify whether the intake sill remains submerged in each selected state.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"製作三種季節工況表，為每列填入同時水位、流量與濃度。將資料缺口列出，說明哪種缺測會妨礙判斷淹沒、泥砂或魚類掃流條件。","textEn":"Create three seasonal scenarios with simultaneous stage, discharge and concentration. Identify missing observations and explain which gaps prevent assessment of submergence, sediment behavior or fish-guiding sweeping flow.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「引水比例與季節工況機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Diversion fraction and seasonal states mechanism and verification\"?","options":["將取水紀錄與同時河川流量配對，分別整理枯水、常水及洪水事件。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","排砂用水越多就必定越有效，而且不用檢查下游再沉積。"],"optionsEn":["Pair diversion records with simultaneous river flow and separate low, ordinary and flood events.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","More flushing water is always more effective and downstream redeposition need not be checked."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將取水紀錄與同時河川流量配對，分別整理枯水、常水及洪水事件。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Pair diversion records with simultaneous river flow and separate low, ordinary and flood events. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b268-v15-04","title":"引水比例與季節工況機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Diversion fraction and seasonal states mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「引水比例與季節工況」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Diversion fraction and seasonal states” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用年平均流量判斷取水比例會掩蓋枯水壓力，將洪水流量和低水位拼接則可能形成不可能工況；未檢查剩餘流量也會把防淤效率與河川功能割裂。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An annual mean conceals low-flow pressure, while combining flood discharge with unrelated low stage may create an impossible scenario. Omitting remaining flow also separates sediment performance from the river functions affected by diversion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例只是整體水量分配，沒有推導局部流線或可容許取水比例；下游需求與許可條件須另由實際資料確認。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Downstream requirements and permission conditions need separate evidence.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要取水量低於年平均河川流量，就不必分析枯水分流。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Diversion below annual mean river flow makes low-flow allocation analysis unnecessary.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用年平均流量判斷取水比例會掩蓋枯水壓力，將洪水流量和低水位拼接則可能形成不可能工況；未檢查剩餘流量也會把防淤效率與河川功能割裂。","textEn":"An annual mean conceals low-flow pressure, while combining flood discharge with unrelated low stage may create an impossible scenario. Omitting remaining flow also separates sediment performance from the river functions affected by diversion.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「引水比例與季節工況機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Diversion fraction and seasonal states mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","用年平均流量判斷取水比例會掩蓋枯水壓力，將洪水流量和低水位拼接則可能形成不可能工況；未檢查剩餘流量也會把防淤效率與河川功能割裂。","取水流量固定時，只量一次濁度就能確定整場泥砂輸入。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","An annual mean conceals low-flow pressure, while combining flood discharge with unrelated low stage may create an impossible scenario.","With constant diversion, one turbidity measurement determines the entire event sediment input."],"answer":1,"explanation":"用年平均流量判斷取水比例會掩蓋枯水壓力，將洪水流量和低水位拼接則可能形成不可能工況；未檢查剩餘流量也會把防淤效率與河川功能割裂。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An annual mean conceals low-flow pressure, while combining flood discharge with unrelated low stage may create an impossible scenario. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b268-v15-05","title":"懸移質輸入帳機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Suspended-sediment input budget mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「懸移質輸入帳」如何影響河岸取水口防淤設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Suspended-sediment input budget” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sediment-resistant river intake design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"進入取水口的懸移質負荷由濃度和流量共同決定，短時高濃度事件可能主導全年清淤量。濁度只有在與現地懸浮固體校正後才能作代理量，粒徑和顏色改變會破壞單一關係；底床推移質另有運移途徑，不能把懸移質帳當成完整泥砂預算。本例假設濃度在事件內固定並代表截面流量加權平均，未含推移質或取水選擇性；事件質量不等於全部沉積量。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「懸移質輸入帳」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Suspended load entering an intake depends on both concentration and discharge, and brief sediment pulses may dominate maintenance demand. Turbidity becomes a proxy only after local calibration against suspended solids; changing size or color can alter that relation. Bed material has a separate transport pathway, so a suspended-load ledger is not a complete sediment budget. The example assumes constant event concentration representative of a flow-weighted section mean, excluding bed load and selective withdrawal. Event mass is not the mass necessarily deposited. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Suspended-sediment input budget” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=2.0 m³/s、C=0.30 kg/m³、事件t=3600 s，輸入泥砂M=QCt=2160 kg。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=2.0 m³/s, concentration C=0.30 kg/m³ and duration t=3600 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「取水流量固定時，只量一次濁度就能確定整場泥砂輸入。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"With constant diversion, one turbidity measurement determines the entire event sediment input.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「懸移質輸入帳」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Suspended-sediment input budget”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-05-k1","title":"懸移質輸入帳機理與驗證","titleEn":"Suspended-sediment input budget mechanism and verification","text":"進入取水口的懸移質負荷由濃度和流量共同決定，短時高濃度事件可能主導全年清淤量。濁度只有在與現地懸浮固體校正後才能作代理量，粒徑和顏色改變會破壞單一關係；底床推移質另有運移途徑，不能把懸移質帳當成完整泥砂預算。","textEn":"Suspended load entering an intake depends on both concentration and discharge, and brief sediment pulses may dominate maintenance demand. Turbidity becomes a proxy only after local calibration against suspended solids; changing size or color can alter that relation.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：取水流量固定時，只量一次濁度就能確定整場泥砂輸入。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: With constant diversion, one turbidity measurement determines the entire event sediment input. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「懸移質輸入帳機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Suspended-sediment input budget mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["取水流量固定時，只量一次濁度就能確定整場泥砂輸入。","斯托克斯沉降式可不分粒徑與濃度直接套用所有河川泥砂。","進入取水口的懸移質負荷由濃度和流量共同決定，短時高濃度事件可能主導全年清淤量。"],"optionsEn":["With constant diversion, one turbidity measurement determines the entire event sediment input.","Stokes settling applies to all river sediment regardless of grain size or concentration.","Suspended load entering an intake depends on both concentration and discharge, and brief sediment pulses may dominate maintenance demand."],"answer":2,"explanation":"進入取水口的懸移質負荷由濃度和流量共同決定，短時高濃度事件可能主導全年清淤量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Suspended load entering an intake depends on both concentration and discharge, and brief sediment pulses may dominate maintenance demand. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b268-v15-06","title":"懸移質輸入帳機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Suspended-sediment input budget mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「懸移質輸入帳」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Suspended-sediment input budget” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=2.0 m³/s、C=0.30 kg/m³、事件t=3600 s，輸入泥砂M=QCt=2160 kg。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=2.0 m³/s, concentration C=0.30 kg/m³ and duration t=3600 s. Incoming sediment M=QCt=2160 kg. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：於上升和退水段採樣並與流量同步，檢查濁度關係是否隨事件或粒徑改變。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Sample rising and falling limbs with synchronized discharge, checking whether turbidity calibration changes by event or grain size.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=2.0 m³/s、C=0.30 kg/m³、事件t=3600 s，輸入泥砂M=QCt=2160 kg。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=2.0 m³/s, concentration C=0.30 kg/m³ and duration t=3600 s. Incoming sediment M=QCt=2160 kg.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「懸移質輸入帳機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Suspended-sediment input budget mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=2.0 m³/s、C=0.30 kg/m³、事件t=3600 s，輸入泥砂M=QCt=2160 kg。","床砂開始動就等於所有泥砂會立即沖走且不會在下游再沉積。","沿篩速度和穿篩速度只差名稱，因此可以互換使用。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=2.0 m³/s, concentration C=0.30 kg/m³ and duration t=3600 s.","Initial bed motion means all sediment immediately flushes away without downstream redeposition.","Sweeping and through-screen velocities differ only in name and can be interchanged."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=2.0 m³/s、C=0.30 kg/m³、事件t=3600 s，輸入泥砂M=QCt=2160 kg。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=2.0 m³/s, concentration C=0.30 kg/m³ and duration t=3600 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b268-v15-07","title":"懸移質輸入帳機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Suspended-sediment input budget mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「懸移質輸入帳」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Suspended-sediment input budget” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"於上升和退水段採樣並與流量同步，檢查濁度關係是否隨事件或粒徑改變。對截面不均勻性與取樣代表性作紀錄，再以進出質量和清淤紀錄核對累積結果。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Sample rising and falling limbs with synchronized discharge, checking whether turbidity calibration changes by event or grain size. Document section nonuniformity and sampling representation, then compare cumulative inputs and outputs with recovered sediment records to evaluate the budget. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用分段濃度序列計算事件質量，與平均濃度乘總體積比較。指出哪個平均必須按流量加權，並將未計入的推移質列為獨立資料需求。","observationEn":"Site practice: Integrate a segmented concentration series and compare it with mean concentration times total volume. Identify the average requiring flow weighting and list excluded bed load as an independent data requirement.","failure":"注意干擾：以單次低濁度樣本外推整場洪水會漏掉峰值負荷，直接把輸入質量全當沉積又會忽略穿越出流；兩種誤差可能相反但不能假設互相抵消。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Extrapolating one low-turbidity sample misses event peaks, while treating all incoming mass as deposited ignores sediment passing through. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"於上升和退水段採樣並與流量同步，檢查濁度關係是否隨事件或粒徑改變。對截面不均勻性與取樣代表性作紀錄，再以進出質量和清淤紀錄核對累積結果。","textEn":"Sample rising and falling limbs with synchronized discharge, checking whether turbidity calibration changes by event or grain size. Document section nonuniformity and sampling representation, then compare cumulative inputs and outputs with recovered sediment records to evaluate the budget.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用分段濃度序列計算事件質量，與平均濃度乘總體積比較。指出哪個平均必須按流量加權，並將未計入的推移質列為獨立資料需求。","textEn":"Integrate a segmented concentration series and compare it with mean concentration times total volume. Identify the average requiring flow weighting and list excluded bed load as an independent data requirement.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「懸移質輸入帳機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Suspended-sediment input budget mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","於上升和退水段採樣並與流量同步，檢查濁度關係是否隨事件或粒徑改變。","清淤間隔只需用總庫容除以全年平均量，不必測局部床形。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Sample rising and falling limbs with synchronized discharge, checking whether turbidity calibration changes by event or grain size.","Maintenance interval needs only total storage divided by annual mean load, without local bed surveys."],"answer":1,"explanation":"於上升和退水段採樣並與流量同步，檢查濁度關係是否隨事件或粒徑改變。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Sample rising and falling limbs with synchronized discharge, checking whether turbidity calibration changes by event or grain size. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b268-v15-08","title":"懸移質輸入帳機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Suspended-sediment input budget mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「懸移質輸入帳」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Suspended-sediment input budget” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以單次低濁度樣本外推整場洪水會漏掉峰值負荷，直接把輸入質量全當沉積又會忽略穿越出流；兩種誤差可能相反但不能假設互相抵消。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Extrapolating one low-turbidity sample misses event peaks, while treating all incoming mass as deposited ignores sediment passing through. These errors can oppose each other but cannot be assumed to cancel. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例假設濃度在事件內固定並代表截面流量加權平均，未含推移質或取水選擇性；事件質量不等於全部沉積量。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Event mass is not the mass necessarily deposited.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「取水流量固定時，只量一次濁度就能確定整場泥砂輸入。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"With constant diversion, one turbidity measurement determines the entire event sediment input.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以單次低濁度樣本外推整場洪水會漏掉峰值負荷，直接把輸入質量全當沉積又會忽略穿越出流；兩種誤差可能相反但不能假設互相抵消。","textEn":"Extrapolating one low-turbidity sample misses event peaks, while treating all incoming mass as deposited ignores sediment passing through. These errors can oppose each other but cannot be assumed to cancel.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「懸移質輸入帳機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Suspended-sediment input budget mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","斯托克斯沉降式可不分粒徑與濃度直接套用所有河川泥砂。","以單次低濁度樣本外推整場洪水會漏掉峰值負荷，直接把輸入質量全當沉積又會忽略穿越出流；兩種誤差可能相反但不能假設互相抵消。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Stokes settling applies to all river sediment regardless of grain size or concentration.","Extrapolating one low-turbidity sample misses event peaks, while treating all incoming mass as deposited ignores sediment passing through."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以單次低濁度樣本外推整場洪水會漏掉峰值負荷，直接把輸入質量全當沉積又會忽略穿越出流；兩種誤差可能相反但不能假設互相抵消。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Extrapolating one low-turbidity sample misses event peaks, while treating all incoming mass as deposited ignores sediment passing through. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b268-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「細粒沉降尺度機理與驗證」與「沉砂池表面負荷機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Fine-particle settling scale mechanism and verification\" and \"Settling-basin surface loading mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b268-v15-09","title":"細粒沉降尺度機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Fine-particle settling scale mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「細粒沉降尺度」如何影響河岸取水口防淤設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Fine-particle settling scale” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sediment-resistant river intake design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"顆粒沉降速度影響取水渠與沉砂區內的分離，但粒徑不是唯一因素，密度、形狀、黏度和絮凝都會改變結果。斯托克斯關係適用低顆粒雷諾數的孤立球形顆粒，不能套用到所有砂粒或高濃度團聚；計算後應回查流態，避免公式假設與所得速度互相矛盾。以下粒徑為二十微米並假設不絮凝、稀薄懸浮；若顆粒雷諾數不小或具黏聚性，需換用適當實測或模型。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「細粒沉降尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Settling speed influences separation in intake channels and basins, but size alone is insufficient: density, shape, viscosity and flocculation also matter. Stokes settling describes isolated spherical particles at low particle Reynolds number, not all sand or concentrated aggregates. The calculated speed must be used to recheck flow regime so that the result does not contradict its assumptions. The example uses twenty-micrometer particles in dilute nonflocculating suspension. Larger particle Reynolds number or cohesive behavior requires suitable measurements or another model. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Fine-particle settling scale” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρs=2650、ρw=1000 kg/m³、d=20 μm、μ=0.001 Pa·s，ws=(ρs−ρw)gd²/(18μ)=0.0003597 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρs=2650, ρw=1000 kg/m³, d=20 μm and μ=0.001 Pa·s.","failure":"常見誤解：「斯托克斯沉降式可不分粒徑與濃度直接套用所有河川泥砂。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Stokes settling applies to all river sediment regardless of grain size or concentration.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「細粒沉降尺度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Fine-particle settling scale”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-09-k1","title":"細粒沉降尺度機理與驗證","titleEn":"Fine-particle settling scale mechanism and verification","text":"顆粒沉降速度影響取水渠與沉砂區內的分離，但粒徑不是唯一因素，密度、形狀、黏度和絮凝都會改變結果。斯托克斯關係適用低顆粒雷諾數的孤立球形顆粒，不能套用到所有砂粒或高濃度團聚；計算後應回查流態，避免公式假設與所得速度互相矛盾。","textEn":"Settling speed influences separation in intake channels and basins, but size alone is insufficient: density, shape, viscosity and flocculation also matter. Stokes settling describes isolated spherical particles at low particle Reynolds number, not all sand or concentrated aggregates.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：斯托克斯沉降式可不分粒徑與濃度直接套用所有河川泥砂。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Stokes settling applies to all river sediment regardless of grain size or concentration. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「細粒沉降尺度機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Fine-particle settling scale mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["顆粒沉降速度影響取水渠與沉砂區內的分離，但粒徑不是唯一因素，密度、形狀、黏度和絮凝都會改變結果。","斯托克斯沉降式可不分粒徑與濃度直接套用所有河川泥砂。","沉砂池只要越深，所有粒徑的理想去除效率就一定越高。"],"optionsEn":["Settling speed influences separation in intake channels and basins, but size alone is insufficient: density, shape, viscosity and flocculation also matter.","Stokes settling applies to all river sediment regardless of grain size or concentration.","A deeper settling basin necessarily improves ideal removal for every grain size."],"answer":0,"explanation":"顆粒沉降速度影響取水渠與沉砂區內的分離，但粒徑不是唯一因素，密度、形狀、黏度和絮凝都會改變結果。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Settling speed influences separation in intake channels and basins, but size alone is insufficient: density, shape, viscosity and flocculation also matter. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b268-v15-10","title":"細粒沉降尺度機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Fine-particle settling scale mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「細粒沉降尺度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Fine-particle settling scale” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρs=2650、ρw=1000 kg/m³、d=20 μm、μ=0.001 Pa·s，ws=(ρs−ρw)gd²/(18μ)=0.0003597 m/s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρs=2650, ρw=1000 kg/m³, d=20 μm and μ=0.001 Pa·s. Stokes ws=(ρs−ρw)gd²/(18μ)=0.0003597 m/s with g=9.81 m/s². Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將微米轉為公尺後重算速度，利用所得值檢查顆粒雷諾數約為零點〇〇七二。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Convert micrometers to meters and recompute speed, then use that result to check a particle Reynolds number of approximately 0.0072.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρs=2650、ρw=1000 kg/m³、d=20 μm、μ=0.001 Pa·s，ws=(ρs−ρw)gd²/(18μ)=0.0003597 m/s。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρs=2650, ρw=1000 kg/m³, d=20 μm and μ=0.001 Pa·s. Stokes ws=(ρs−ρw)gd²/(18μ)=0.0003597 m/s with g=9.81 m/s².","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「細粒沉降尺度機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Fine-particle settling scale mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["均勻流平均剪應力就是每個角落與閘門下方的真實床面應力。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρs=2650、ρw=1000 kg/m³、d=20 μm、μ=0.001 Pa·s，ws=(ρs−ρw)gd²/(18μ)=0.0003597 m/s。","排砂用水越多就必定越有效，而且不用檢查下游再沉積。"],"optionsEn":["Uniform-flow mean shear equals actual bed stress in every corner and beneath every gate.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρs=2650, ρw=1000 kg/m³, d=20 μm and μ=0.001 Pa·s.","More flushing water is always more effective and downstream redeposition need not be checked."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρs=2650、ρw=1000 kg/m³、d=20 μm、μ=0.001 Pa·s，ws=(ρs−ρw)gd²/(18μ)=0.0003597 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρs=2650, ρw=1000 kg/m³, d=20 μm and μ=0.001 Pa·s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b268-v15-11","title":"細粒沉降尺度機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Fine-particle settling scale mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「細粒沉降尺度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Fine-particle settling scale” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將微米轉為公尺後重算速度，利用所得值檢查顆粒雷諾數約為零點〇〇七二。用沉降柱或代表水樣觀察絮凝及濃度效應，區分理想單粒速度與實際群體沉降。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Convert micrometers to meters and recompute speed, then use that result to check a particle Reynolds number of approximately 0.0072. Examine flocculation and concentration effects with settling-column observations or representative samples, distinguishing ideal single-particle from bulk settling behavior. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：將粒徑增加一倍並計算理想速度與雷諾數變化，說明何時需要停止沿用低雷諾數公式。比較單粒礦砂和絮體試驗需要控制的不同條件。","observationEn":"Site practice: Double diameter and calculate the ideal changes in speed and Reynolds number, explaining when the low-Reynolds formula should no longer be retained. Compare experimental controls required for mineral particles and flocs.","failure":"注意干擾：把微米直接當公尺會造成巨大的平方誤差，將斯托克斯式用於粗砂則會忽略阻力流態改變；有機絮體的有效密度和形狀也不等於礦物球粒。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using micrometers as meters creates a huge squared-unit error, while applying Stokes law to coarse sand ignores changing drag regime. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將微米轉為公尺後重算速度，利用所得值檢查顆粒雷諾數約為零點〇〇七二。用沉降柱或代表水樣觀察絮凝及濃度效應，區分理想單粒速度與實際群體沉降。","textEn":"Convert micrometers to meters and recompute speed, then use that result to check a particle Reynolds number of approximately 0.0072. Examine flocculation and concentration effects with settling-column observations or representative samples, distinguishing ideal single-particle from bulk settling behavior.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"將粒徑增加一倍並計算理想速度與雷諾數變化，說明何時需要停止沿用低雷諾數公式。比較單粒礦砂和絮體試驗需要控制的不同條件。","textEn":"Double diameter and calculate the ideal changes in speed and Reynolds number, explaining when the low-Reynolds formula should no longer be retained. Compare experimental controls required for mineral particles and flocs.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「細粒沉降尺度機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Fine-particle settling scale mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","水工模型保持福祿數後，泥砂起動和所有魚類行為就自然相似。","將微米轉為公尺後重算速度，利用所得值檢查顆粒雷諾數約為零點〇〇七二。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Preserving Froude number automatically preserves sediment motion and all fish behavior.","Convert micrometers to meters and recompute speed, then use that result to check a particle Reynolds number of approximately 0.0072."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將微米轉為公尺後重算速度，利用所得值檢查顆粒雷諾數約為零點〇〇七二。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Convert micrometers to meters and recompute speed, then use that result to check a particle Reynolds number of approximately 0.0072. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b268-v15-12","title":"細粒沉降尺度機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Fine-particle settling scale mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「細粒沉降尺度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Fine-particle settling scale” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把微米直接當公尺會造成巨大的平方誤差，將斯托克斯式用於粗砂則會忽略阻力流態改變；有機絮體的有效密度和形狀也不等於礦物球粒。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using micrometers as meters creates a huge squared-unit error, while applying Stokes law to coarse sand ignores changing drag regime. Organic flocs also have effective density and shape unlike mineral spheres. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：以下粒徑為二十微米並假設不絮凝、稀薄懸浮；若顆粒雷諾數不小或具黏聚性，需換用適當實測或模型。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Larger particle Reynolds number or cohesive behavior requires suitable measurements or another model.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「斯托克斯沉降式可不分粒徑與濃度直接套用所有河川泥砂。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Stokes settling applies to all river sediment regardless of grain size or concentration.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把微米直接當公尺會造成巨大的平方誤差，將斯托克斯式用於粗砂則會忽略阻力流態改變；有機絮體的有效密度和形狀也不等於礦物球粒。","textEn":"Using micrometers as meters creates a huge squared-unit error, while applying Stokes law to coarse sand ignores changing drag regime. Organic flocs also have effective density and shape unlike mineral spheres.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「細粒沉降尺度機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Fine-particle settling scale mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["把微米直接當公尺會造成巨大的平方誤差，將斯托克斯式用於粗砂則會忽略阻力流態改變；有機絮體的有效密度和形狀也不等於礦物球粒。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","沉砂池只要越深，所有粒徑的理想去除效率就一定越高。"],"optionsEn":["Using micrometers as meters creates a huge squared-unit error, while applying Stokes law to coarse sand ignores changing drag regime.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A deeper settling basin necessarily improves ideal removal for every grain size."],"answer":0,"explanation":"把微米直接當公尺會造成巨大的平方誤差，將斯托克斯式用於粗砂則會忽略阻力流態改變；有機絮體的有效密度和形狀也不等於礦物球粒。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using micrometers as meters creates a huge squared-unit error, while applying Stokes law to coarse sand ignores changing drag regime. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b268-v15-13","title":"沉砂池表面負荷機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Settling-basin surface loading mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「沉砂池表面負荷」如何影響河岸取水口防淤設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Settling-basin surface loading” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sediment-resistant river intake design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"理想水平流沉砂池中，顆粒能否落到底部取決於沉降速度與表面溢流負荷的比較，而不只是池深。增加深度同時增加沉降距離與停留時間，不能在其他條件不變時保證理想去除率提高；短路流、入口紊動與再懸浮會使實際表現偏離理想粒子軌跡。本例只求表面負荷並與指定單粒速度比較，假設均勻穩定流；不將理論臨界值當成全粒徑的實際去除率。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「沉砂池表面負荷」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"In an ideal horizontal-flow basin, settling depends on the comparison of particle settling speed with surface overflow loading, not depth alone. Greater depth increases both settling distance and residence time and therefore does not automatically improve ideal removal at unchanged plan area and flow. Short-circuiting, inlet turbulence and resuspension cause departures from ideal particle trajectories. The example calculates surface loading against a specified settling speed under uniform steady flow. It does not turn a theoretical cutoff into actual removal for every grain class. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Settling-basin surface loading” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=0.20 m³/s、平面面積A=100 m²，表面負荷vo=Q/A=0.0020 m/s；指定ws=0.003 m/s大於vo。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=0.20 m³/s and plan area A=100 m².","failure":"常見誤解：「沉砂池只要越深，所有粒徑的理想去除效率就一定越高。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A deeper settling basin necessarily improves ideal removal for every grain size.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「沉砂池表面負荷」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Settling-basin surface loading”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-13-k1","title":"沉砂池表面負荷機理與驗證","titleEn":"Settling-basin surface loading mechanism and verification","text":"理想水平流沉砂池中，顆粒能否落到底部取決於沉降速度與表面溢流負荷的比較，而不只是池深。增加深度同時增加沉降距離與停留時間，不能在其他條件不變時保證理想去除率提高；短路流、入口紊動與再懸浮會使實際表現偏離理想粒子軌跡。","textEn":"In an ideal horizontal-flow basin, settling depends on the comparison of particle settling speed with surface overflow loading, not depth alone. Greater depth increases both settling distance and residence time and therefore does not automatically improve ideal removal at unchanged plan area and flow.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：沉砂池只要越深，所有粒徑的理想去除效率就一定越高。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A deeper settling basin necessarily improves ideal removal for every grain size. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「沉砂池表面負荷機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Settling-basin surface loading mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["沉砂池只要越深，所有粒徑的理想去除效率就一定越高。","理想水平流沉砂池中，顆粒能否落到底部取決於沉降速度與表面溢流負荷的比較，而不只是池深。","床砂開始動就等於所有泥砂會立即沖走且不會在下游再沉積。"],"optionsEn":["A deeper settling basin necessarily improves ideal removal for every grain size.","In an ideal horizontal-flow basin, settling depends on the comparison of particle settling speed with surface overflow loading, not depth alone.","Initial bed motion means all sediment immediately flushes away without downstream redeposition."],"answer":1,"explanation":"理想水平流沉砂池中，顆粒能否落到底部取決於沉降速度與表面溢流負荷的比較，而不只是池深。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"In an ideal horizontal-flow basin, settling depends on the comparison of particle settling speed with surface overflow loading, not depth alone. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b268-v15-14","title":"沉砂池表面負荷機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Settling-basin surface loading mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「沉砂池表面負荷」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Settling-basin surface loading” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=0.20 m³/s、平面面積A=100 m²，表面負荷vo=Q/A=0.0020 m/s；指定ws=0.003 m/s大於vo。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=0.20 m³/s and plan area A=100 m². Surface loading vo=Q/A=0.0020 m/s; specified ws=0.003 m/s exceeds vo. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對有效平面面積及進出口流量，利用示蹤或速度分布檢查短路與死區。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check effective plan area and inlet/outlet flow, using tracer or velocity measurements to detect short circuits and dead zones.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=0.20 m³/s、平面面積A=100 m²，表面負荷vo=Q/A=0.0020 m/s；指定ws=0.003 m/s大於vo。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=0.20 m³/s and plan area A=100 m². Surface loading vo=Q/A=0.0020 m/s; specified ws=0.003 m/s exceeds vo.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「沉砂池表面負荷機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Settling-basin surface loading mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["沿篩速度和穿篩速度只差名稱，因此可以互換使用。","清淤間隔只需用總庫容除以全年平均量，不必測局部床形。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=0.20 m³/s、平面面積A=100 m²，表面負荷vo=Q/A=0.0020 m/s。"],"optionsEn":["Sweeping and through-screen velocities differ only in name and can be interchanged.","Maintenance interval needs only total storage divided by annual mean load, without local bed surveys.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=0.20 m³/s and plan area A=100 m²."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設Q=0.20 m³/s、平面面積A=100 m²，表面負荷vo=Q/A=0.0020 m/s；指定ws=0.003 m/s大於vo。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume Q=0.20 m³/s and plan area A=100 m². Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b268-v15-15","title":"沉砂池表面負荷機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Settling-basin surface loading mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「沉砂池表面負荷」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Settling-basin surface loading” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對有效平面面積及進出口流量，利用示蹤或速度分布檢查短路與死區。依粒徑分組比較進出濃度，再觀察清淤前後是否因床面抬高造成再懸浮或入口擾動。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check effective plan area and inlet/outlet flow, using tracer or velocity measurements to detect short circuits and dead zones. Compare incoming and outgoing concentration by size class, then inspect whether deposited material alters resuspension or inlet disturbance before and after cleaning. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：固定流量比較增加面積與增加深度兩種方案，分別計算表面負荷和停留時間。指出理想模型無法描述的入口短路，並規劃一個可檢查它的示蹤觀察。","observationEn":"Site practice: At fixed flow compare added area with added depth, calculating surface loading and residence time separately. Identify inlet short-circuiting absent from the ideal model and plan a tracer observation capable of detecting it.","failure":"注意干擾：只加深沉砂池而不處理短路流可能幾乎沒有改善，堆積泥砂還會縮小有效空間；把單粒理想條件直接報成整體去除百分率會掩蓋粒徑分布。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Deepening a basin without addressing short-circuiting may offer little benefit, while sediment deposits shrink its effective space. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對有效平面面積及進出口流量，利用示蹤或速度分布檢查短路與死區。依粒徑分組比較進出濃度，再觀察清淤前後是否因床面抬高造成再懸浮或入口擾動。","textEn":"Check effective plan area and inlet/outlet flow, using tracer or velocity measurements to detect short circuits and dead zones. Compare incoming and outgoing concentration by size class, then inspect whether deposited material alters resuspension or inlet disturbance before and after cleaning.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"固定流量比較增加面積與增加深度兩種方案，分別計算表面負荷和停留時間。指出理想模型無法描述的入口短路，並規劃一個可檢查它的示蹤觀察。","textEn":"At fixed flow compare added area with added depth, calculating surface loading and residence time separately. Identify inlet short-circuiting absent from the ideal model and plan a tracer observation capable of detecting it.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「沉砂池表面負荷機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Settling-basin surface loading mechanism and verification\"?","options":["核對有效平面面積及進出口流量，利用示蹤或速度分布檢查短路與死區。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","只要取水量低於年平均河川流量，就不必分析枯水分流。"],"optionsEn":["Check effective plan area and inlet/outlet flow, using tracer or velocity measurements to detect short circuits and dead zones.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Diversion below annual mean river flow makes low-flow allocation analysis unnecessary."],"answer":0,"explanation":"核對有效平面面積及進出口流量，利用示蹤或速度分布檢查短路與死區。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check effective plan area and inlet/outlet flow, using tracer or velocity measurements to detect short circuits and dead zones. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b268-v15-16","title":"沉砂池表面負荷機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Settling-basin surface loading mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「沉砂池表面負荷」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Settling-basin surface loading” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只加深沉砂池而不處理短路流可能幾乎沒有改善，堆積泥砂還會縮小有效空間；把單粒理想條件直接報成整體去除百分率會掩蓋粒徑分布。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Deepening a basin without addressing short-circuiting may offer little benefit, while sediment deposits shrink its effective space. Reporting a single-particle ideal condition as overall removal percentage conceals the incoming grain-size distribution. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例只求表面負荷並與指定單粒速度比較，假設均勻穩定流；不將理論臨界值當成全粒徑的實際去除率。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It does not turn a theoretical cutoff into actual removal for every grain class.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「沉砂池只要越深，所有粒徑的理想去除效率就一定越高。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A deeper settling basin necessarily improves ideal removal for every grain size.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只加深沉砂池而不處理短路流可能幾乎沒有改善，堆積泥砂還會縮小有效空間；把單粒理想條件直接報成整體去除百分率會掩蓋粒徑分布。","textEn":"Deepening a basin without addressing short-circuiting may offer little benefit, while sediment deposits shrink its effective space. Reporting a single-particle ideal condition as overall removal percentage conceals the incoming grain-size distribution.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「沉砂池表面負荷機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Settling-basin surface loading mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只加深沉砂池而不處理短路流可能幾乎沒有改善，堆積泥砂還會縮小有效空間；把單粒理想條件直接報成整體去除百分率會掩蓋粒徑分布。","床砂開始動就等於所有泥砂會立即沖走且不會在下游再沉積。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Deepening a basin without addressing short-circuiting may offer little benefit, while sediment deposits shrink its effective space.","Initial bed motion means all sediment immediately flushes away without downstream redeposition."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只加深沉砂池而不處理短路流可能幾乎沒有改善，堆積泥砂還會縮小有效空間；把單粒理想條件直接報成整體去除百分率會掩蓋粒徑分布。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Deepening a basin without addressing short-circuiting may offer little benefit, while sediment deposits shrink its effective space. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b268-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「非黏性顆粒起動機理與驗證」與「沖砂渠床面應力機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Noncohesive incipient motion mechanism and verification\" and \"Flushing-channel bed stress mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b268-v15-17","title":"非黏性顆粒起動機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Noncohesive incipient motion mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「非黏性顆粒起動」如何影響河岸取水口防淤設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Noncohesive incipient motion” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sediment-resistant river intake design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"沖砂能力可先由床面剪應力與顆粒抗移尺度比較，但起動不是固定流速一到就所有顆粒一起移動。無量綱希爾茲參數受粒徑、黏度、床面坡度與顆粒遮蔽影響，混合粒床還會有護甲效應；黏土的侵蝕則涉及黏聚與固結，不能沿用相同單粒非黏性判準。本例的臨界希爾茲數是指定假設，只用於水平、均勻非黏性床比較；未由此預測輸砂率或沖砂完成時間。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「非黏性顆粒起動」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Flushing potential can first be compared through bed shear and particle-resistance scales, but motion does not begin simultaneously for every grain at one fixed velocity. Shields behavior depends on size, viscosity, bed slope and hiding, while mixed beds can armor. Cohesive erosion also depends on bonding and consolidation and cannot reuse the same noncohesive single-grain criterion. The critical Shields value is an assumed input for a horizontal uniform noncohesive bed. It predicts neither sediment transport rate nor time to complete flushing. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Noncohesive incipient motion” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設θc=0.05、ρs=2650、ρw=1000 kg/m³、d=0.001 m，τc=θc(ρs−ρw)gd=0.8093 Pa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume θc=0.05, ρs=2650, ρw=1000 kg/m³ and d=0.001 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「床砂開始動就等於所有泥砂會立即沖走且不會在下游再沉積。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Initial bed motion means all sediment immediately flushes away without downstream redeposition.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「非黏性顆粒起動」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Noncohesive incipient motion”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-17-k1","title":"非黏性顆粒起動機理與驗證","titleEn":"Noncohesive incipient motion mechanism and verification","text":"沖砂能力可先由床面剪應力與顆粒抗移尺度比較，但起動不是固定流速一到就所有顆粒一起移動。無量綱希爾茲參數受粒徑、黏度、床面坡度與顆粒遮蔽影響，混合粒床還會有護甲效應；黏土的侵蝕則涉及黏聚與固結，不能沿用相同單粒非黏性判準。","textEn":"Flushing potential can first be compared through bed shear and particle-resistance scales, but motion does not begin simultaneously for every grain at one fixed velocity. Shields behavior depends on size, viscosity, bed slope and hiding, while mixed beds can armor.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：床砂開始動就等於所有泥砂會立即沖走且不會在下游再沉積。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Initial bed motion means all sediment immediately flushes away without downstream redeposition. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「非黏性顆粒起動機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Noncohesive incipient motion mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["床砂開始動就等於所有泥砂會立即沖走且不會在下游再沉積。","均勻流平均剪應力就是每個角落與閘門下方的真實床面應力。","沖砂能力可先由床面剪應力與顆粒抗移尺度比較，但起動不是固定流速一到就所有顆粒一起移動。"],"optionsEn":["Initial bed motion means all sediment immediately flushes away without downstream redeposition.","Uniform-flow mean shear equals actual bed stress in every corner and beneath every gate.","Flushing potential can first be compared through bed shear and particle-resistance scales, but motion does not begin simultaneously for every grain at one fixed velocity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"沖砂能力可先由床面剪應力與顆粒抗移尺度比較，但起動不是固定流速一到就所有顆粒一起移動。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Flushing potential can first be compared through bed shear and particle-resistance scales, but motion does not begin simultaneously for every grain at one fixed velocity. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b268-v15-18","title":"非黏性顆粒起動機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Noncohesive incipient motion mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「非黏性顆粒起動」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Noncohesive incipient motion” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設θc=0.05、ρs=2650、ρw=1000 kg/m³、d=0.001 m，τc=θc(ρs−ρw)gd=0.8093 Pa。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume θc=0.05, ρs=2650, ρw=1000 kg/m³ and d=0.001 m. Critical τc=θc(ρs−ρw)gd=0.8093 Pa at g=9.81 m/s². Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：調查床砂粒徑與黏性成分，核對臨界參數來源的粒徑及流態範圍。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Survey grain distribution and cohesive content, checking the source parameter’s grain and flow-regime range.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設θc=0.05、ρs=2650、ρw=1000 kg/m³、d=0.001 m，τc=θc(ρs−ρw)gd=0.8093 Pa。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume θc=0.05, ρs=2650, ρw=1000 kg/m³ and d=0.001 m. Critical τc=θc(ρs−ρw)gd=0.8093 Pa at g=9.81 m/s².","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「非黏性顆粒起動機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Noncohesive incipient motion mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設θc=0.05、ρs=2650、ρw=1000 kg/m³、d=0.001 m，τc=θc(ρs−ρw)gd=0.8093 Pa。","排砂用水越多就必定越有效，而且不用檢查下游再沉積。","水工模型保持福祿數後，泥砂起動和所有魚類行為就自然相似。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume θc=0.05, ρs=2650, ρw=1000 kg/m³ and d=0.001 m.","More flushing water is always more effective and downstream redeposition need not be checked.","Preserving Froude number automatically preserves sediment motion and all fish behavior."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設θc=0.05、ρs=2650、ρw=1000 kg/m³、d=0.001 m，τc=θc(ρs−ρw)gd=0.8093 Pa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume θc=0.05, ρs=2650, ρw=1000 kg/m³ and d=0.001 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b268-v15-19","title":"非黏性顆粒起動機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Noncohesive incipient motion mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「非黏性顆粒起動」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Noncohesive incipient motion” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"調查床砂粒徑與黏性成分，核對臨界參數來源的粒徑及流態範圍。將模型床面應力與起動觀察比較，保留護甲和局部坡度證據，再判斷是否需要多粒徑或黏性侵蝕模型。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Survey grain distribution and cohesive content, checking the source parameter’s grain and flow-regime range. Compare modeled bed stress with observed onset, retain evidence of armoring and local slope, then decide whether multiple-size or cohesive-erosion modeling is required. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：用兩種假設粒徑比較臨界應力，再將含黏土的第三種材料標為公式範圍外。畫出由起動到輸送出口的路徑，列出每段仍需驗證的條件。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare critical stress for two assumed grain sizes and mark a third clay-bearing material outside the formula’s scope. Draw the path from initial motion to outlet transport, identifying conditions still requiring verification along each reach.","failure":"注意干擾：把非黏性常數套用固結淤泥會錯估沖砂需求，將平均應力當所有位置應力也會漏掉低速堆積區；達到起動條件仍不保證泥砂能通過下游出口。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Applying a noncohesive constant to consolidated mud misstates flushing demand, and treating mean stress as universal misses low-velocity deposits. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"調查床砂粒徑與黏性成分，核對臨界參數來源的粒徑及流態範圍。將模型床面應力與起動觀察比較，保留護甲和局部坡度證據，再判斷是否需要多粒徑或黏性侵蝕模型。","textEn":"Survey grain distribution and cohesive content, checking the source parameter’s grain and flow-regime range. Compare modeled bed stress with observed onset, retain evidence of armoring and local slope, then decide whether multiple-size or cohesive-erosion modeling is required.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"用兩種假設粒徑比較臨界應力，再將含黏土的第三種材料標為公式範圍外。畫出由起動到輸送出口的路徑，列出每段仍需驗證的條件。","textEn":"Compare critical stress for two assumed grain sizes and mark a third clay-bearing material outside the formula’s scope. Draw the path from initial motion to outlet transport, identifying conditions still requiring verification along each reach.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「非黏性顆粒起動機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Noncohesive incipient motion mechanism and verification\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","調查床砂粒徑與黏性成分，核對臨界參數來源的粒徑及流態範圍。","取水流量固定時，只量一次濁度就能確定整場泥砂輸入。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Survey grain distribution and cohesive content, checking the source parameter’s grain and flow-regime range.","With constant diversion, one turbidity measurement determines the entire event sediment input."],"answer":1,"explanation":"調查床砂粒徑與黏性成分，核對臨界參數來源的粒徑及流態範圍。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Survey grain distribution and cohesive content, checking the source parameter’s grain and flow-regime range. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b268-v15-20","title":"非黏性顆粒起動機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Noncohesive incipient motion mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「非黏性顆粒起動」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Noncohesive incipient motion” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把非黏性常數套用固結淤泥會錯估沖砂需求，將平均應力當所有位置應力也會漏掉低速堆積區；達到起動條件仍不保證泥砂能通過下游出口。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Applying a noncohesive constant to consolidated mud misstates flushing demand, and treating mean stress as universal misses low-velocity deposits. Reaching incipient motion does not guarantee that sediment can travel through the downstream outlet. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例的臨界希爾茲數是指定假設，只用於水平、均勻非黏性床比較；未由此預測輸砂率或沖砂完成時間。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It predicts neither sediment transport rate nor time to complete flushing.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「床砂開始動就等於所有泥砂會立即沖走且不會在下游再沉積。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Initial bed motion means all sediment immediately flushes away without downstream redeposition.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把非黏性常數套用固結淤泥會錯估沖砂需求，將平均應力當所有位置應力也會漏掉低速堆積區；達到起動條件仍不保證泥砂能通過下游出口。","textEn":"Applying a noncohesive constant to consolidated mud misstates flushing demand, and treating mean stress as universal misses low-velocity deposits. Reaching incipient motion does not guarantee that sediment can travel through the downstream outlet.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「非黏性顆粒起動機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Noncohesive incipient motion mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","均勻流平均剪應力就是每個角落與閘門下方的真實床面應力。","把非黏性常數套用固結淤泥會錯估沖砂需求，將平均應力當所有位置應力也會漏掉低速堆積區；達到起動條件仍不保證泥砂能通過下游出口。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Uniform-flow mean shear equals actual bed stress in every corner and beneath every gate.","Applying a noncohesive constant to consolidated mud misstates flushing demand, and treating mean stress as universal misses low-velocity deposits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把非黏性常數套用固結淤泥會錯估沖砂需求，將平均應力當所有位置應力也會漏掉低速堆積區；達到起動條件仍不保證泥砂能通過下游出口。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Applying a noncohesive constant to consolidated mud misstates flushing demand, and treating mean stress as universal misses low-velocity deposits. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b268-v15-21","title":"沖砂渠床面應力機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Flushing-channel bed stress mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「沖砂渠床面應力」如何影響河岸取水口防淤設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Flushing-channel bed stress” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sediment-resistant river intake design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"均勻明渠流的平均邊界應力可用水力半徑和能量坡降估算，適合作為沖砂能力的初步尺度。取水口附近的彎流、收縮和閘下射流通常不均勻，局部床面剪應力可能與周界平均值差很大；若用水面坡度代替能量坡度，還必須先確認沿程加速度與損失分布。本例假設穩定均勻流，所得為平均邊界應力；不能把它直接指定給取水口角落、彎道外岸或閘下局部沖刷。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「沖砂渠床面應力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Uniform open-channel flow permits a mean boundary-stress estimate from hydraulic radius and energy slope, providing an initial flushing scale. Bends, contractions and gate jets near intakes are nonuniform, so local bed stress can differ substantially from the wetted-perimeter mean. Substituting water-surface slope for energy slope additionally requires checking acceleration and the distribution of losses. The example assumes steady uniform flow and yields mean boundary stress. It cannot directly prescribe stress at intake corners, outer bends or local scour beneath a gate. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Flushing-channel bed stress” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²、水力半徑R=0.50 m、能坡Sf=0.001，τ=ρgRSf=4.905 Pa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρ=1000 kg/m³, g=9.81 m/s², hydraulic radius R=0.50 m and energy slope Sf=0.001.","failure":"常見誤解：「均勻流平均剪應力就是每個角落與閘門下方的真實床面應力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Uniform-flow mean shear equals actual bed stress in every corner and beneath every gate.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「沖砂渠床面應力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Flushing-channel bed stress”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-21-k1","title":"沖砂渠床面應力機理與驗證","titleEn":"Flushing-channel bed stress mechanism and verification","text":"均勻明渠流的平均邊界應力可用水力半徑和能量坡降估算，適合作為沖砂能力的初步尺度。取水口附近的彎流、收縮和閘下射流通常不均勻，局部床面剪應力可能與周界平均值差很大；若用水面坡度代替能量坡度，還必須先確認沿程加速度與損失分布。","textEn":"Uniform open-channel flow permits a mean boundary-stress estimate from hydraulic radius and energy slope, providing an initial flushing scale. Bends, contractions and gate jets near intakes are nonuniform, so local bed stress can differ substantially from the wetted-perimeter mean.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：均勻流平均剪應力就是每個角落與閘門下方的真實床面應力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Uniform-flow mean shear equals actual bed stress in every corner and beneath every gate. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「沖砂渠床面應力機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Flushing-channel bed stress mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["均勻明渠流的平均邊界應力可用水力半徑和能量坡降估算，適合作為沖砂能力的初步尺度。","均勻流平均剪應力就是每個角落與閘門下方的真實床面應力。","沿篩速度和穿篩速度只差名稱，因此可以互換使用。"],"optionsEn":["Uniform open-channel flow permits a mean boundary-stress estimate from hydraulic radius and energy slope, providing an initial flushing scale.","Uniform-flow mean shear equals actual bed stress in every corner and beneath every gate.","Sweeping and through-screen velocities differ only in name and can be interchanged."],"answer":0,"explanation":"均勻明渠流的平均邊界應力可用水力半徑和能量坡降估算，適合作為沖砂能力的初步尺度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Uniform open-channel flow permits a mean boundary-stress estimate from hydraulic radius and energy slope, providing an initial flushing scale. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b268-v15-22","title":"沖砂渠床面應力機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Flushing-channel bed stress mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「沖砂渠床面應力」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Flushing-channel bed stress” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²、水力半徑R=0.50 m、能坡Sf=0.001，τ=ρgRSf=4.905 Pa。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρ=1000 kg/m³, g=9.81 m/s², hydraulic radius R=0.50 m and energy slope Sf=0.001. Mean stress τ=ρgRSf=4.905 Pa. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量測渠段斷面與水面高程，核對流況是否接近均勻並估計能量項。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure channel sections and water-surface elevations, assess proximity to uniform flow and account for energy terms.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²、水力半徑R=0.50 m、能坡Sf=0.001，τ=ρgRSf=4.905 Pa。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρ=1000 kg/m³, g=9.81 m/s², hydraulic radius R=0.50 m and energy slope Sf=0.001. Mean stress τ=ρgRSf=4.905 Pa.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「沖砂渠床面應力機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Flushing-channel bed stress mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["清淤間隔只需用總庫容除以全年平均量，不必測局部床形。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²、水力半徑R=0.50 m、能坡Sf=0.001，τ=ρgRSf=4.905 Pa。","只要取水量低於年平均河川流量，就不必分析枯水分流。"],"optionsEn":["Maintenance interval needs only total storage divided by annual mean load, without local bed surveys.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρ=1000 kg/m³, g=9.81 m/s², hydraulic radius R=0.50 m and energy slope Sf=0.001.","Diversion below annual mean river flow makes low-flow allocation analysis unnecessary."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²、水力半徑R=0.50 m、能坡Sf=0.001，τ=ρgRSf=4.905 Pa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume ρ=1000 kg/m³, g=9.81 m/s², hydraulic radius R=0.50 m and energy slope Sf=0.001. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b268-v15-23","title":"沖砂渠床面應力機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Flushing-channel bed stress mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「沖砂渠床面應力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Flushing-channel bed stress” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量測渠段斷面與水面高程，核對流況是否接近均勻並估計能量項。對轉彎、死角及閘下區另用局部速度或模型檢查應力，不能只以全渠平均值驗證清淤效果。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure channel sections and water-surface elevations, assess proximity to uniform flow and account for energy terms. Examine bends, dead zones and gate-jet regions with local velocities or modeling instead of using one channel-average value to verify sediment-clearing performance everywhere. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：計算平均應力後，在平面圖標示可能較低或較高的局部區域。為每個區域選擇可驗證的速度或床形觀察，說明為何它不能被平均值取代。","observationEn":"Site practice: After calculating mean stress, mark potentially lower and higher local zones on a plan. Select velocity or bed-form observations for each zone and explain why the mean cannot replace these local measurements.","failure":"注意干擾：以平均應力高於臨界值就宣稱全渠無淤積，會漏掉死區及分流口；提高沖砂水量也可能把沖刷風險轉移到結構基礎或下游河岸。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Declaring the whole channel sediment-free because average stress exceeds a threshold overlooks dead zones and branching entrances. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量測渠段斷面與水面高程，核對流況是否接近均勻並估計能量項。對轉彎、死角及閘下區另用局部速度或模型檢查應力，不能只以全渠平均值驗證清淤效果。","textEn":"Measure channel sections and water-surface elevations, assess proximity to uniform flow and account for energy terms. Examine bends, dead zones and gate-jet regions with local velocities or modeling instead of using one channel-average value to verify sediment-clearing performance everywhere.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"計算平均應力後，在平面圖標示可能較低或較高的局部區域。為每個區域選擇可驗證的速度或床形觀察，說明為何它不能被平均值取代。","textEn":"After calculating mean stress, mark potentially lower and higher local zones on a plan. Select velocity or bed-form observations for each zone and explain why the mean cannot replace these local measurements.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「沖砂渠床面應力機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Flushing-channel bed stress mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","斯托克斯沉降式可不分粒徑與濃度直接套用所有河川泥砂。","量測渠段斷面與水面高程，核對流況是否接近均勻並估計能量項。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Stokes settling applies to all river sediment regardless of grain size or concentration.","Measure channel sections and water-surface elevations, assess proximity to uniform flow and account for energy terms."],"answer":2,"explanation":"量測渠段斷面與水面高程，核對流況是否接近均勻並估計能量項。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure channel sections and water-surface elevations, assess proximity to uniform flow and account for energy terms. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b268-v15-24","title":"沖砂渠床面應力機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Flushing-channel bed stress mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「沖砂渠床面應力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Flushing-channel bed stress” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以平均應力高於臨界值就宣稱全渠無淤積，會漏掉死區及分流口；提高沖砂水量也可能把沖刷風險轉移到結構基礎或下游河岸。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Declaring the whole channel sediment-free because average stress exceeds a threshold overlooks dead zones and branching entrances. Increasing flushing discharge can also transfer erosion risk to structural foundations or downstream riverbanks. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例假設穩定均勻流，所得為平均邊界應力；不能把它直接指定給取水口角落、彎道外岸或閘下局部沖刷。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It cannot directly prescribe stress at intake corners, outer bends or local scour beneath a gate.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「均勻流平均剪應力就是每個角落與閘門下方的真實床面應力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Uniform-flow mean shear equals actual bed stress in every corner and beneath every gate.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以平均應力高於臨界值就宣稱全渠無淤積，會漏掉死區及分流口；提高沖砂水量也可能把沖刷風險轉移到結構基礎或下游河岸。","textEn":"Declaring the whole channel sediment-free because average stress exceeds a threshold overlooks dead zones and branching entrances. Increasing flushing discharge can also transfer erosion risk to structural foundations or downstream riverbanks.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「沖砂渠床面應力機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Flushing-channel bed stress mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["以平均應力高於臨界值就宣稱全渠無淤積，會漏掉死區及分流口；提高沖砂水量也可能把沖刷風險轉移到結構基礎或下游河岸。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","沿篩速度和穿篩速度只差名稱，因此可以互換使用。"],"optionsEn":["Declaring the whole channel sediment-free because average stress exceeds a threshold overlooks dead zones and branching entrances.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Sweeping and through-screen velocities differ only in name and can be interchanged."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以平均應力高於臨界值就宣稱全渠無淤積，會漏掉死區及分流口；提高沖砂水量也可能把沖刷風險轉移到結構基礎或下游河岸。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Declaring the whole channel sediment-free because average stress exceeds a threshold overlooks dead zones and branching entrances. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b268-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「篩網方向與掃流機理與驗證」與「沖砂水量與事件管理機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Screen orientation and sweeping flow mechanism and verification\" and \"Flushing volume and event management mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b268-v15-25","title":"篩網方向與掃流機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Screen orientation and sweeping flow mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「篩網方向與掃流」如何影響河岸取水口防淤設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Screen orientation and sweeping flow” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sediment-resistant river intake design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"河岸篩網的防淤與魚類導引都受到來流方向影響，總速度應分成垂直篩面的接近分量和沿面的掃流分量。改變角度可能減少法向吸入但增加設施長度，且實際河流有垂向和橫向不均；簡單向量分解只能描述指定位置，不能替代整片篩面的速度普查。本例角度明確定義為流向相對篩面切線的夾角，未把假設速度當魚種標準；接近速度的量測位置須依評估方法指定。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「篩網方向與掃流」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Screen sediment behavior and fish guidance depend on approach direction, requiring separation of normal approach velocity from tangential sweeping velocity. Reorientation may reduce normal entry while increasing structure length, and real rivers have vertical and lateral variation. A vector decomposition describes one location only and cannot replace a spatial velocity survey across the screen. The angle is measured from the screen tangent to the flow direction, and the assumed speed is not a species criterion. Measurement offset must follow the selected evaluation method. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Screen orientation and sweeping flow” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設來流V=0.50 m/s、與篩面切線夾角α=20°，法向Vn=Vsinα=0.1710 m/s，沿面Vs=Vcosα=0.4698 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume flow V=0.50 m/s at α=20° from the screen tangent.","failure":"常見誤解：「沿篩速度和穿篩速度只差名稱，因此可以互換使用。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Sweeping and through-screen velocities differ only in name and can be interchanged.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「篩網方向與掃流」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Screen orientation and sweeping flow”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-25-k1","title":"篩網方向與掃流機理與驗證","titleEn":"Screen orientation and sweeping flow mechanism and verification","text":"河岸篩網的防淤與魚類導引都受到來流方向影響，總速度應分成垂直篩面的接近分量和沿面的掃流分量。改變角度可能減少法向吸入但增加設施長度，且實際河流有垂向和橫向不均；簡單向量分解只能描述指定位置，不能替代整片篩面的速度普查。","textEn":"Screen sediment behavior and fish guidance depend on approach direction, requiring separation of normal approach velocity from tangential sweeping velocity. Reorientation may reduce normal entry while increasing structure length, and real rivers have vertical and lateral variation.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：沿篩速度和穿篩速度只差名稱，因此可以互換使用。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Sweeping and through-screen velocities differ only in name and can be interchanged. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「篩網方向與掃流機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Screen orientation and sweeping flow mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["沿篩速度和穿篩速度只差名稱，因此可以互換使用。","河岸篩網的防淤與魚類導引都受到來流方向影響，總速度應分成垂直篩面的接近分量和沿面的掃流分量。","排砂用水越多就必定越有效，而且不用檢查下游再沉積。"],"optionsEn":["Sweeping and through-screen velocities differ only in name and can be interchanged.","Screen sediment behavior and fish guidance depend on approach direction, requiring separation of normal approach velocity from tangential sweeping velocity.","More flushing water is always more effective and downstream redeposition need not be checked."],"answer":1,"explanation":"河岸篩網的防淤與魚類導引都受到來流方向影響，總速度應分成垂直篩面的接近分量和沿面的掃流分量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Screen sediment behavior and fish guidance depend on approach direction, requiring separation of normal approach velocity from tangential sweeping velocity. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b268-v15-26","title":"篩網方向與掃流機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Screen orientation and sweeping flow mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「篩網方向與掃流」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Screen orientation and sweeping flow” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設來流V=0.50 m/s、與篩面切線夾角α=20°，法向Vn=Vsinα=0.1710 m/s，沿面Vs=Vcosα=0.4698 m/s。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume flow V=0.50 m/s at α=20° from the screen tangent. Normal Vn=Vsinα=0.1710 m/s and sweeping Vs=Vcosα=0.4698 m/s. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在測點圖標明篩面切線、法線及感測器方向，依相同離面距離量測速度分量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Mark screen tangent, normal and sensor orientation on the survey map, measuring components at consistent offsets.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設來流V=0.50 m/s、與篩面切線夾角α=20°，法向Vn=Vsinα=0.1710 m/s，沿面Vs=Vcosα=0.4698 m/s。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume flow V=0.50 m/s at α=20° from the screen tangent. Normal Vn=Vsinα=0.1710 m/s and sweeping Vs=Vcosα=0.4698 m/s.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「篩網方向與掃流機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Screen orientation and sweeping flow mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["水工模型保持福祿數後，泥砂起動和所有魚類行為就自然相似。","取水流量固定時，只量一次濁度就能確定整場泥砂輸入。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設來流V=0.50 m/s、與篩面切線夾角α=20°，法向Vn=Vsinα=0.1710 m/s，沿面Vs=Vcosα=0.4698 m/s。"],"optionsEn":["Preserving Froude number automatically preserves sediment motion and all fish behavior.","With constant diversion, one turbidity measurement determines the entire event sediment input.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume flow V=0.50 m/s at α=20° from the screen tangent."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設來流V=0.50 m/s、與篩面切線夾角α=20°，法向Vn=Vsinα=0.1710 m/s，沿面Vs=Vcosα=0.4698 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume flow V=0.50 m/s at α=20° from the screen tangent. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b268-v15-27","title":"篩網方向與掃流機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Screen orientation and sweeping flow mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「篩網方向與掃流」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Screen orientation and sweeping flow” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在測點圖標明篩面切線、法線及感測器方向，依相同離面距離量測速度分量。將面積積分流量與取水計量核對，並在堵塞、低水位與不同機組運轉下重查熱點。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Mark screen tangent, normal and sensor orientation on the survey map, measuring components at consistent offsets. Reconcile area-integrated flow with intake metering and revisit hotspots under blockage, low water and different pump combinations to check spatial representation. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：為同一來流畫出兩個篩面角度並分解速度，清楚標記角度起算方向。指出幾何比較之外仍需驗證的旁通入口、局部堵塞與物種條件。","observationEn":"Site practice: Draw two screen angles for the same incoming flow and resolve velocities, explicitly marking the angle reference. Identify bypass-entry, local-blockage and species conditions that still need checking beyond the geometric comparison.","failure":"注意干擾：把角度從法線量卻套切線公式會交換兩個分量，局部高速區可能因此被低估；只報平均掃流也無法證明魚類可順利到達旁通出口。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Measuring angle from the normal but using tangent-based formulas swaps components and can understate hotspots. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在測點圖標明篩面切線、法線及感測器方向，依相同離面距離量測速度分量。將面積積分流量與取水計量核對，並在堵塞、低水位與不同機組運轉下重查熱點。","textEn":"Mark screen tangent, normal and sensor orientation on the survey map, measuring components at consistent offsets. Reconcile area-integrated flow with intake metering and revisit hotspots under blockage, low water and different pump combinations to check spatial representation.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"為同一來流畫出兩個篩面角度並分解速度，清楚標記角度起算方向。指出幾何比較之外仍需驗證的旁通入口、局部堵塞與物種條件。","textEn":"Draw two screen angles for the same incoming flow and resolve velocities, explicitly marking the angle reference. Identify bypass-entry, local-blockage and species conditions that still need checking beyond the geometric comparison.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「篩網方向與掃流機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Screen orientation and sweeping flow mechanism and verification\"?","options":["在測點圖標明篩面切線、法線及感測器方向，依相同離面距離量測速度分量。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","沉砂池只要越深，所有粒徑的理想去除效率就一定越高。"],"optionsEn":["Mark screen tangent, normal and sensor orientation on the survey map, measuring components at consistent offsets.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A deeper settling basin necessarily improves ideal removal for every grain size."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在測點圖標明篩面切線、法線及感測器方向，依相同離面距離量測速度分量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Mark screen tangent, normal and sensor orientation on the survey map, measuring components at consistent offsets. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b268-v15-28","title":"篩網方向與掃流機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Screen orientation and sweeping flow mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「篩網方向與掃流」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Screen orientation and sweeping flow” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把角度從法線量卻套切線公式會交換兩個分量，局部高速區可能因此被低估；只報平均掃流也無法證明魚類可順利到達旁通出口。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Measuring angle from the normal but using tangent-based formulas swaps components and can understate hotspots. Reporting mean sweeping velocity alone also does not establish successful movement to the bypass outlet. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例角度明確定義為流向相對篩面切線的夾角，未把假設速度當魚種標準；接近速度的量測位置須依評估方法指定。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Measurement offset must follow the selected evaluation method.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「沿篩速度和穿篩速度只差名稱，因此可以互換使用。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Sweeping and through-screen velocities differ only in name and can be interchanged.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把角度從法線量卻套切線公式會交換兩個分量，局部高速區可能因此被低估；只報平均掃流也無法證明魚類可順利到達旁通出口。","textEn":"Measuring angle from the normal but using tangent-based formulas swaps components and can understate hotspots. Reporting mean sweeping velocity alone also does not establish successful movement to the bypass outlet.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「篩網方向與掃流機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Screen orientation and sweeping flow mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","把角度從法線量卻套切線公式會交換兩個分量，局部高速區可能因此被低估；只報平均掃流也無法證明魚類可順利到達旁通出口。","排砂用水越多就必定越有效，而且不用檢查下游再沉積。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Measuring angle from the normal but using tangent-based formulas swaps components and can understate hotspots.","More flushing water is always more effective and downstream redeposition need not be checked."],"answer":1,"explanation":"把角度從法線量卻套切線公式會交換兩個分量，局部高速區可能因此被低估；只報平均掃流也無法證明魚類可順利到達旁通出口。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Measuring angle from the normal but using tangent-based formulas swaps components and can understate hotspots. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b268-v15-29","title":"沖砂水量與事件管理機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Flushing volume and event management mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「沖砂水量與事件管理」如何影響河岸取水口防淤設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Flushing volume and event management” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sediment-resistant river intake design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"沖砂不是只要閘門開啟就完成，水量、持續時間和下游輸送能力共同決定效果。短時大流量可能啟動床砂卻在出口形成新沉積，長時低流量則可能不足以維持運移；用水帳還須與供水和河川需求協調，不能把排砂水當作沒有代價的額外資源。本例只求指定穩定排砂流量的總水體積，不預測泥砂去除率，也不建議任何現場開閘順序或時間設定。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「沖砂水量與事件管理」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Opening a gate does not by itself complete sediment flushing. Flow, duration and downstream transport capacity determine performance. A brief large release may mobilize material that redeposits at the outlet, while prolonged low flow may not sustain movement. The water budget must also account for supply and river needs rather than treating flushing water as a free additional resource. The example calculates water volume for a specified constant flushing flow, not sediment removal efficiency. It gives no field gate-opening sequence or operating-time recommendation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Flushing volume and event management” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設排砂流量Qf=3.0 m³/s、持續t=600 s，使用水量V=Qft=1800 m³。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume flushing flow Qf=3.0 m³/s for t=600 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「排砂用水越多就必定越有效，而且不用檢查下游再沉積。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"More flushing water is always more effective and downstream redeposition need not be checked.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「沖砂水量與事件管理」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Flushing volume and event management”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-29-k1","title":"沖砂水量與事件管理機理與驗證","titleEn":"Flushing volume and event management mechanism and verification","text":"沖砂不是只要閘門開啟就完成，水量、持續時間和下游輸送能力共同決定效果。短時大流量可能啟動床砂卻在出口形成新沉積，長時低流量則可能不足以維持運移；用水帳還須與供水和河川需求協調，不能把排砂水當作沒有代價的額外資源。","textEn":"Opening a gate does not by itself complete sediment flushing. Flow, duration and downstream transport capacity determine performance.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：排砂用水越多就必定越有效，而且不用檢查下游再沉積。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: More flushing water is always more effective and downstream redeposition need not be checked. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「沖砂水量與事件管理機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Flushing volume and event management mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["排砂用水越多就必定越有效，而且不用檢查下游再沉積。","清淤間隔只需用總庫容除以全年平均量，不必測局部床形。","沖砂不是只要閘門開啟就完成，水量、持續時間和下游輸送能力共同決定效果。"],"optionsEn":["More flushing water is always more effective and downstream redeposition need not be checked.","Maintenance interval needs only total storage divided by annual mean load, without local bed surveys.","Opening a gate does not by itself complete sediment flushing."],"answer":2,"explanation":"沖砂不是只要閘門開啟就完成，水量、持續時間和下游輸送能力共同決定效果。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Opening a gate does not by itself complete sediment flushing. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b268-v15-30","title":"沖砂水量與事件管理機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Flushing volume and event management mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「沖砂水量與事件管理」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Flushing volume and event management” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設排砂流量Qf=3.0 m³/s、持續t=600 s，使用水量V=Qft=1800 m³。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume flushing flow Qf=3.0 m³/s for t=600 s. Water volume V=Qft=1800 m³. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將排砂前後地形和出流泥砂濃度對時，核對實際水量與輸出質量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Align before-and-after bathymetry with outgoing sediment concentration, checking actual water volume and exported mass.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設排砂流量Qf=3.0 m³/s、持續t=600 s，使用水量V=Qft=1800 m³。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume flushing flow Qf=3.0 m³/s for t=600 s. Water volume V=Qft=1800 m³.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「沖砂水量與事件管理機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Flushing volume and event management mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設排砂流量Qf=3.0 m³/s、持續t=600 s，使用水量V=Qft=1800 m³。","只要取水量低於年平均河川流量，就不必分析枯水分流。","斯托克斯沉降式可不分粒徑與濃度直接套用所有河川泥砂。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume flushing flow Qf=3.0 m³/s for t=600 s.","Diversion below annual mean river flow makes low-flow allocation analysis unnecessary.","Stokes settling applies to all river sediment regardless of grain size or concentration."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設排砂流量Qf=3.0 m³/s、持續t=600 s，使用水量V=Qft=1800 m³。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume flushing flow Qf=3.0 m³/s for t=600 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b268-v15-31","title":"沖砂水量與事件管理機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Flushing volume and event management mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「沖砂水量與事件管理」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Flushing volume and event management” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將排砂前後地形和出流泥砂濃度對時，核對實際水量與輸出質量。另觀察下游沉積、濁度及供水變化，確認移走的泥砂沒有只轉移到另一個敏感或阻塞位置。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Align before-and-after bathymetry with outgoing sediment concentration, checking actual water volume and exported mass. Observe downstream deposits, turbidity and supply changes to establish whether removed sediment has merely shifted to another sensitive location or potential blockage rather than leaving the system. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：建立一次假設排砂的水量、泥砂輸出與床形變化三本帳。說明三者不一致時可能是取樣、密度換算或泥砂轉移問題，並提出可區分原因的觀察。","observationEn":"Site practice: Create separate ledgers for flushing water, exported sediment and bed-volume change. Explain how disagreement can reflect sampling, density conversion or relocation, and propose observations that distinguish those possible causes.","failure":"注意干擾：以耗水量大就推定沖砂有效會忽略低速死區，未檢查下游則可能把取水口的問題搬到河道；沖砂後供水恢復也不能證明所有沉積已清除。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: High water use does not prove effective flushing in low-velocity dead zones. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將排砂前後地形和出流泥砂濃度對時，核對實際水量與輸出質量。另觀察下游沉積、濁度及供水變化，確認移走的泥砂沒有只轉移到另一個敏感或阻塞位置。","textEn":"Align before-and-after bathymetry with outgoing sediment concentration, checking actual water volume and exported mass. Observe downstream deposits, turbidity and supply changes to establish whether removed sediment has merely shifted to another sensitive location or potential blockage rather than leaving the system.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"建立一次假設排砂的水量、泥砂輸出與床形變化三本帳。說明三者不一致時可能是取樣、密度換算或泥砂轉移問題，並提出可區分原因的觀察。","textEn":"Create separate ledgers for flushing water, exported sediment and bed-volume change. Explain how disagreement can reflect sampling, density conversion or relocation, and propose observations that distinguish those possible causes.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「沖砂水量與事件管理機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Flushing volume and event management mechanism and verification\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","將排砂前後地形和出流泥砂濃度對時，核對實際水量與輸出質量。","床砂開始動就等於所有泥砂會立即沖走且不會在下游再沉積。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Align before-and-after bathymetry with outgoing sediment concentration, checking actual water volume and exported mass.","Initial bed motion means all sediment immediately flushes away without downstream redeposition."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將排砂前後地形和出流泥砂濃度對時，核對實際水量與輸出質量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Align before-and-after bathymetry with outgoing sediment concentration, checking actual water volume and exported mass. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b268-v15-32","title":"沖砂水量與事件管理機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Flushing volume and event management mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「沖砂水量與事件管理」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Flushing volume and event management” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以耗水量大就推定沖砂有效會忽略低速死區，未檢查下游則可能把取水口的問題搬到河道；沖砂後供水恢復也不能證明所有沉積已清除。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"High water use does not prove effective flushing in low-velocity dead zones. Without downstream checks the intake problem may simply move into the river, and restored supply does not demonstrate complete sediment removal. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例只求指定穩定排砂流量的總水體積，不預測泥砂去除率，也不建議任何現場開閘順序或時間設定。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: It gives no field gate-opening sequence or operating-time recommendation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「排砂用水越多就必定越有效，而且不用檢查下游再沉積。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"More flushing water is always more effective and downstream redeposition need not be checked.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以耗水量大就推定沖砂有效會忽略低速死區，未檢查下游則可能把取水口的問題搬到河道；沖砂後供水恢復也不能證明所有沉積已清除。","textEn":"High water use does not prove effective flushing in low-velocity dead zones. Without downstream checks the intake problem may simply move into the river, and restored supply does not demonstrate complete sediment removal.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「沖砂水量與事件管理機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Flushing volume and event management mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","清淤間隔只需用總庫容除以全年平均量，不必測局部床形。","以耗水量大就推定沖砂有效會忽略低速死區，未檢查下游則可能把取水口的問題搬到河道；沖砂後供水恢復也不能證明所有沉積已清除。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Maintenance interval needs only total storage divided by annual mean load, without local bed surveys.","High water use does not prove effective flushing in low-velocity dead zones."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以耗水量大就推定沖砂有效會忽略低速死區，未檢查下游則可能把取水口的問題搬到河道；沖砂後供水恢復也不能證明所有沉積已清除。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"High water use does not prove effective flushing in low-velocity dead zones. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b268-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「沉積庫容與清淤頻率機理與驗證」與「實體模型相似限制機理與驗證」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Deposit storage and maintenance interval mechanism and verification\" and \"Physical-model similarity limits mechanism and verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b268-v15-33","title":"沉積庫容與清淤頻率機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Deposit storage and maintenance interval mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「沉積庫容與清淤頻率」如何影響河岸取水口防淤設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Deposit storage and maintenance interval” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sediment-resistant river intake design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"沉砂設施需要把固體質量換成含孔隙的沉積體積，才可估計可用庫容與清理需求。顆粒密度不是沉積乾容重，孔隙、含水與固結會改變體積；平均沉積率只提供規劃尺度，洪水脈衝和空間不均可能使局部高程先達限制，不能只等總庫容耗盡。本例採乾固體質量和指定乾容重，忽略固結與事件變動；算得間隔是線性庫容比較，並非實際維護排程。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「沉積庫容與清淤頻率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Sediment storage planning converts solid mass into deposit volume including pores. Grain density is not dry bulk density, and porosity, water content and consolidation alter volume. A mean deposition rate gives a planning scale only: flood pulses and uneven deposits can reach local elevation constraints before total nominal storage is exhausted. The example uses dry solid mass and specified dry bulk density, excluding consolidation and event variability. The interval is a linear storage comparison, not an actual maintenance schedule. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Deposit storage and maintenance interval” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設日沉積乾質量Md=1200 kg/day、乾容重ρd=1500 kg/m³，日體積0.80 m³/day；可用容積40 m³對應50 day。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume deposited dry mass Md=1200 kg/day and dry bulk density ρd=1500 kg/m³.","failure":"常見誤解：「清淤間隔只需用總庫容除以全年平均量，不必測局部床形。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Maintenance interval needs only total storage divided by annual mean load, without local bed surveys.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「沉積庫容與清淤頻率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Deposit storage and maintenance interval”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-33-k1","title":"沉積庫容與清淤頻率機理與驗證","titleEn":"Deposit storage and maintenance interval mechanism and verification","text":"沉砂設施需要把固體質量換成含孔隙的沉積體積，才可估計可用庫容與清理需求。顆粒密度不是沉積乾容重，孔隙、含水與固結會改變體積；平均沉積率只提供規劃尺度，洪水脈衝和空間不均可能使局部高程先達限制，不能只等總庫容耗盡。","textEn":"Sediment storage planning converts solid mass into deposit volume including pores. Grain density is not dry bulk density, and porosity, water content and consolidation alter volume.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：清淤間隔只需用總庫容除以全年平均量，不必測局部床形。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Maintenance interval needs only total storage divided by annual mean load, without local bed surveys. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「沉積庫容與清淤頻率機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Deposit storage and maintenance interval mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["沉砂設施需要把固體質量換成含孔隙的沉積體積，才可估計可用庫容與清理需求。","清淤間隔只需用總庫容除以全年平均量，不必測局部床形。","水工模型保持福祿數後，泥砂起動和所有魚類行為就自然相似。"],"optionsEn":["Sediment storage planning converts solid mass into deposit volume including pores.","Maintenance interval needs only total storage divided by annual mean load, without local bed surveys.","Preserving Froude number automatically preserves sediment motion and all fish behavior."],"answer":0,"explanation":"沉砂設施需要把固體質量換成含孔隙的沉積體積，才可估計可用庫容與清理需求。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Sediment storage planning converts solid mass into deposit volume including pores. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b268-v15-34","title":"沉積庫容與清淤頻率機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Deposit storage and maintenance interval mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「沉積庫容與清淤頻率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Deposit storage and maintenance interval” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設日沉積乾質量Md=1200 kg/day、乾容重ρd=1500 kg/m³，日體積0.80 m³/day；可用容積40 m³對應50 day。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume deposited dry mass Md=1200 kg/day and dry bulk density ρd=1500 kg/m³. Volume is 0.80 m³/day; 40 m³ usable storage corresponds to 50 days. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以代表樣本量測乾容重並以測深確認沉積分布，將清理量、事件負荷與剩餘庫容交叉比對。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure representative dry bulk density and map deposit distribution, comparing removed volume, event loads and remaining storage.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設日沉積乾質量Md=1200 kg/day、乾容重ρd=1500 kg/m³，日體積0.80 m³/day；可用容積40 m³對應50 day。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume deposited dry mass Md=1200 kg/day and dry bulk density ρd=1500 kg/m³. Volume is 0.80 m³/day; 40 m³ usable storage corresponds to 50 days.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「沉積庫容與清淤頻率機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Deposit storage and maintenance interval mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["取水流量固定時，只量一次濁度就能確定整場泥砂輸入。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設日沉積乾質量Md=1200 kg/day、乾容重ρd=1500 kg/m³，日體積0.80 m³/day。","沉砂池只要越深，所有粒徑的理想去除效率就一定越高。"],"optionsEn":["With constant diversion, one turbidity measurement determines the entire event sediment input.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume deposited dry mass Md=1200 kg/day and dry bulk density ρd=1500 kg/m³.","A deeper settling basin necessarily improves ideal removal for every grain size."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設日沉積乾質量Md=1200 kg/day、乾容重ρd=1500 kg/m³，日體積0.80 m³/day；可用容積40 m³對應50 day。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume deposited dry mass Md=1200 kg/day and dry bulk density ρd=1500 kg/m³. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b268-v15-35","title":"沉積庫容與清淤頻率機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Deposit storage and maintenance interval mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「沉積庫容與清淤頻率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Deposit storage and maintenance interval” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以代表樣本量測乾容重並以測深確認沉積分布，將清理量、事件負荷與剩餘庫容交叉比對。對門檻與取水附近設局部高程檢查，避免用總體積掩蓋關鍵區域先被填滿。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure representative dry bulk density and map deposit distribution, comparing removed volume, event loads and remaining storage. Check local elevations near sills and intake openings so that a total-volume ledger does not conceal critical areas filling before the nominal capacity is reached. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：比較相同固體質量在兩種乾容重下的體積，再加入一次假設洪水脈衝。指出庫容帳和局部床形檢查各回答什麼問題，設計可更新間隔的資料表。","observationEn":"Site practice: Compare deposit volumes at two dry bulk densities, then add a hypothetical flood pulse. Explain the distinct questions answered by storage accounting and local bathymetry, and create a record that supports updating the interval.","failure":"注意干擾：用礦物密度代替乾容重會低估堆積體積，以平均日量推算固定清淤日可能漏掉一次大洪水；局部堆積抬高即使總庫容仍足夠也能妨礙取水。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using grain density instead of dry bulk density understates deposit volume, and a fixed date based on mean daily load can miss a major flood pulse. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以代表樣本量測乾容重並以測深確認沉積分布，將清理量、事件負荷與剩餘庫容交叉比對。對門檻與取水附近設局部高程檢查，避免用總體積掩蓋關鍵區域先被填滿。","textEn":"Measure representative dry bulk density and map deposit distribution, comparing removed volume, event loads and remaining storage. Check local elevations near sills and intake openings so that a total-volume ledger does not conceal critical areas filling before the nominal capacity is reached.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"比較相同固體質量在兩種乾容重下的體積，再加入一次假設洪水脈衝。指出庫容帳和局部床形檢查各回答什麼問題，設計可更新間隔的資料表。","textEn":"Compare deposit volumes at two dry bulk densities, then add a hypothetical flood pulse. Explain the distinct questions answered by storage accounting and local bathymetry, and create a record that supports updating the interval.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「沉積庫容與清淤頻率機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Deposit storage and maintenance interval mechanism and verification\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","均勻流平均剪應力就是每個角落與閘門下方的真實床面應力。","以代表樣本量測乾容重並以測深確認沉積分布，將清理量、事件負荷與剩餘庫容交叉比對。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Uniform-flow mean shear equals actual bed stress in every corner and beneath every gate.","Measure representative dry bulk density and map deposit distribution, comparing removed volume, event loads and remaining storage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以代表樣本量測乾容重並以測深確認沉積分布，將清理量、事件負荷與剩餘庫容交叉比對。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure representative dry bulk density and map deposit distribution, comparing removed volume, event loads and remaining storage. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b268-v15-36","title":"沉積庫容與清淤頻率機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Deposit storage and maintenance interval mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「沉積庫容與清淤頻率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Deposit storage and maintenance interval” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"用礦物密度代替乾容重會低估堆積體積，以平均日量推算固定清淤日可能漏掉一次大洪水；局部堆積抬高即使總庫容仍足夠也能妨礙取水。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using grain density instead of dry bulk density understates deposit volume, and a fixed date based on mean daily load can miss a major flood pulse. Local buildup may obstruct diversion while overall storage remains available. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例採乾固體質量和指定乾容重，忽略固結與事件變動；算得間隔是線性庫容比較，並非實際維護排程。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The interval is a linear storage comparison, not an actual maintenance schedule.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「清淤間隔只需用總庫容除以全年平均量，不必測局部床形。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Maintenance interval needs only total storage divided by annual mean load, without local bed surveys.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"用礦物密度代替乾容重會低估堆積體積，以平均日量推算固定清淤日可能漏掉一次大洪水；局部堆積抬高即使總庫容仍足夠也能妨礙取水。","textEn":"Using grain density instead of dry bulk density understates deposit volume, and a fixed date based on mean daily load can miss a major flood pulse. Local buildup may obstruct diversion while overall storage remains available.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「沉積庫容與清淤頻率機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Deposit storage and maintenance interval mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["用礦物密度代替乾容重會低估堆積體積，以平均日量推算固定清淤日可能漏掉一次大洪水；局部堆積抬高即使總庫容仍足夠也能妨礙取水。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","水工模型保持福祿數後，泥砂起動和所有魚類行為就自然相似。"],"optionsEn":["Using grain density instead of dry bulk density understates deposit volume, and a fixed date based on mean daily load can miss a major flood pulse.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Preserving Froude number automatically preserves sediment motion and all fish behavior."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用礦物密度代替乾容重會低估堆積體積，以平均日量推算固定清淤日可能漏掉一次大洪水；局部堆積抬高即使總庫容仍足夠也能妨礙取水。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using grain density instead of dry bulk density understates deposit volume, and a fixed date based on mean daily load can miss a major flood pulse. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b268-v15-37","title":"實體模型相似限制機理與驗證：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Physical-model similarity limits mechanism and verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「實體模型相似限制」如何影響河岸取水口防淤設計的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Physical-model similarity limits” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Sediment-resistant river intake design”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"縮尺水工模型常優先保持重力與慣性相似，以觀察水面、分流和旋渦，但泥砂運移還受黏性、粒徑與密度控制。幾何縮小不代表原型砂粒能按相同比例直接替換，否則沉降與起動可能失真；清水流場試驗可以驗證水力部分，不能自動宣稱防淤與生態功能都已驗證。本例定義長度比為模型除以原型，採福祿相似求速度與流量比；未宣稱雷諾相似或可動床相似同時成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「實體模型相似限制」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Hydraulic scale models often preserve gravity-inertia similarity to examine water levels, flow division and vortices, while sediment transport also depends on viscosity, grain size and density. Geometric reduction does not guarantee proportionally scaled grains reproduce settling and motion. A clear-water experiment can verify hydraulic behavior without automatically validating sediment exclusion or ecological performance. Length ratio is model divided by prototype. Froude similarity supplies velocity and discharge ratios without claiming simultaneous Reynolds or mobile-bed similarity. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Physical-model similarity limits” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設長度比λL=1/25，福祿相似λV=√λL=1/5，流量比λQ=λL^(5/2)=1/3125。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume length ratio λL=1/25.","failure":"常見誤解：「水工模型保持福祿數後，泥砂起動和所有魚類行為就自然相似。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Preserving Froude number automatically preserves sediment motion and all fish behavior.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「實體模型相似限制」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Physical-model similarity limits”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-37-k1","title":"實體模型相似限制機理與驗證","titleEn":"Physical-model similarity limits mechanism and verification","text":"縮尺水工模型常優先保持重力與慣性相似，以觀察水面、分流和旋渦，但泥砂運移還受黏性、粒徑與密度控制。幾何縮小不代表原型砂粒能按相同比例直接替換，否則沉降與起動可能失真；清水流場試驗可以驗證水力部分，不能自動宣稱防淤與生態功能都已驗證。","textEn":"Hydraulic scale models often preserve gravity-inertia similarity to examine water levels, flow division and vortices, while sediment transport also depends on viscosity, grain size and density. Geometric reduction does not guarantee proportionally scaled grains reproduce settling and motion.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：水工模型保持福祿數後，泥砂起動和所有魚類行為就自然相似。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Preserving Froude number automatically preserves sediment motion and all fish behavior. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「實體模型相似限制機理與驗證」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Physical-model similarity limits mechanism and verification\" is correct?","options":["水工模型保持福祿數後，泥砂起動和所有魚類行為就自然相似。","縮尺水工模型常優先保持重力與慣性相似，以觀察水面、分流和旋渦，但泥砂運移還受黏性、粒徑與密度控制。","只要取水量低於年平均河川流量，就不必分析枯水分流。"],"optionsEn":["Preserving Froude number automatically preserves sediment motion and all fish behavior.","Hydraulic scale models often preserve gravity-inertia similarity to examine water levels, flow division and vortices, while sediment transport also depends on viscosity, grain size and density.","Diversion below annual mean river flow makes low-flow allocation analysis unnecessary."],"answer":1,"explanation":"縮尺水工模型常優先保持重力與慣性相似，以觀察水面、分流和旋渦，但泥砂運移還受黏性、粒徑與密度控制。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Hydraulic scale models often preserve gravity-inertia similarity to examine water levels, flow division and vortices, while sediment transport also depends on viscosity, grain size and density. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b268-v15-38","title":"實體模型相似限制機理與驗證：定量估算","titleEn":"Physical-model similarity limits mechanism and verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「實體模型相似限制」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Physical-model similarity limits” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設長度比λL=1/25，福祿相似λV=√λL=1/5，流量比λQ=λL^(5/2)=1/3125。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume length ratio λL=1/25. Under Froude similarity λV=√λL=1/5 and discharge ratio λQ=λL^(5/2)=1/3125. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在試驗計畫分開列出已保持與失真的無量綱群，核對模型流量、粗糙度和量測解析度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: List preserved and distorted dimensionless groups separately, checking model flow, roughness and measurement resolution.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設長度比λL=1/25，福祿相似λV=√λL=1/5，流量比λQ=λL^(5/2)=1/3125。","textEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume length ratio λL=1/25. Under Froude similarity λV=√λL=1/5 and discharge ratio λQ=λL^(5/2)=1/3125.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「實體模型相似限制機理與驗證」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Physical-model similarity limits mechanism and verification\", which statement holds?","options":["斯托克斯沉降式可不分粒徑與濃度直接套用所有河川泥砂。","床砂開始動就等於所有泥砂會立即沖走且不會在下游再沉積。","原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設長度比λL=1/25，福祿相似λV=√λL=1/5，流量比λQ=λL^(5/2)=1/3125。"],"optionsEn":["Stokes settling applies to all river sediment regardless of grain size or concentration.","Initial bed motion means all sediment immediately flushes away without downstream redeposition.","Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume length ratio λL=1/25."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設算例，以下量值用於簡化機理比較：假設長度比λL=1/25，福祿相似λV=√λL=1/5，流量比λQ=λL^(5/2)=1/3125。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching example using hypothetical inputs to compare a simplified physical mechanism: Assume length ratio λL=1/25. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b268-v15-39","title":"實體模型相似限制機理與驗證：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Physical-model similarity limits mechanism and verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「實體模型相似限制」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Physical-model similarity limits” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在試驗計畫分開列出已保持與失真的無量綱群，核對模型流量、粗糙度和量測解析度。若加入可動床，另驗證起動與沉降尺度，並用原型觀測檢查放大後的預測。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"List preserved and distorted dimensionless groups separately, checking model flow, roughness and measurement resolution. If a mobile bed is added, verify motion and settling scales independently, and compare scaled predictions with prototype observations rather than assuming geometric similarity guarantees sediment similarity. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：為指定縮尺計算速度與流量比，再列出雷諾數和沉降尺度需要的額外資料。把水力、可動床與魚類觀察分成三個驗證問題，避免以同一試驗全數代替。","observationEn":"Site practice: Calculate velocity and discharge ratios for the selected scale, then list additional information needed for Reynolds and settling scales. Separate hydraulic, mobile-bed and fish observations into three verification questions instead of claiming one experiment answers all.","failure":"注意干擾：只按幾何比縮砂會讓黏性與黏聚效應變得相對重要，過小模型也可能落入不同流態；忽略這些失真會把清水試驗的漂亮流線誤當成可靠排砂證據。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Scaling grains geometrically can make viscosity and cohesion disproportionately important, and a small model may enter a different flow regime. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在試驗計畫分開列出已保持與失真的無量綱群，核對模型流量、粗糙度和量測解析度。若加入可動床，另驗證起動與沉降尺度，並用原型觀測檢查放大後的預測。","textEn":"List preserved and distorted dimensionless groups separately, checking model flow, roughness and measurement resolution. If a mobile bed is added, verify motion and settling scales independently, and compare scaled predictions with prototype observations rather than assuming geometric similarity guarantees sediment similarity.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"為指定縮尺計算速度與流量比，再列出雷諾數和沉降尺度需要的額外資料。把水力、可動床與魚類觀察分成三個驗證問題，避免以同一試驗全數代替。","textEn":"Calculate velocity and discharge ratios for the selected scale, then list additional information needed for Reynolds and settling scales. Separate hydraulic, mobile-bed and fish observations into three verification questions instead of claiming one experiment answers all.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「實體模型相似限制機理與驗證」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Physical-model similarity limits mechanism and verification\"?","options":["在試驗計畫分開列出已保持與失真的無量綱群，核對模型流量、粗糙度和量測解析度。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","沿篩速度和穿篩速度只差名稱，因此可以互換使用。"],"optionsEn":["List preserved and distorted dimensionless groups separately, checking model flow, roughness and measurement resolution.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Sweeping and through-screen velocities differ only in name and can be interchanged."],"answer":0,"explanation":"在試驗計畫分開列出已保持與失真的無量綱群，核對模型流量、粗糙度和量測解析度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"List preserved and distorted dimensionless groups separately, checking model flow, roughness and measurement resolution. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b268-v15-40","title":"實體模型相似限制機理與驗證：失效診斷","titleEn":"Physical-model similarity limits mechanism and verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"prerequisiteIds":["b268-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「實體模型相似限制」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Physical-model similarity limits” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只按幾何比縮砂會讓黏性與黏聚效應變得相對重要，過小模型也可能落入不同流態；忽略這些失真會把清水試驗的漂亮流線誤當成可靠排砂證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Scaling grains geometrically can make viscosity and cohesion disproportionately important, and a small model may enter a different flow regime. Ignoring these distortions turns attractive clear-water streamlines into unjustified evidence of sediment-removal performance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：本例定義長度比為模型除以原型，採福祿相似求速度與流量比；未宣稱雷諾相似或可動床相似同時成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Froude similarity supplies velocity and discharge ratios without claiming simultaneous Reynolds or mobile-bed similarity.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「水工模型保持福祿數後，泥砂起動和所有魚類行為就自然相似。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Preserving Froude number automatically preserves sediment motion and all fish behavior.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b268-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只按幾何比縮砂會讓黏性與黏聚效應變得相對重要，過小模型也可能落入不同流態；忽略這些失真會把清水試驗的漂亮流線誤當成可靠排砂證據。","textEn":"Scaling grains geometrically can make viscosity and cohesion disproportionately important, and a small model may enter a different flow regime. Ignoring these distortions turns attractive clear-water streamlines into unjustified evidence of sediment-removal performance.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]},{"id":"b268-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「實體模型相似限制機理與驗證」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Physical-model similarity limits mechanism and verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只按幾何比縮砂會讓黏性與黏聚效應變得相對重要，過小模型也可能落入不同流態；忽略這些失真會把清水試驗的漂亮流線誤當成可靠排砂證據。","只要取水量低於年平均河川流量，就不必分析枯水分流。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Scaling grains geometrically can make viscosity and cohesion disproportionately important, and a small model may enter a different flow regime.","Diversion below annual mean river flow makes low-flow allocation analysis unnecessary."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只按幾何比縮砂會讓黏性與黏聚效應變得相對重要，過小模型也可能落入不同流態；忽略這些失真會把清水試驗的漂亮流線誤當成可靠排砂證據。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Scaling grains geometrically can make viscosity and cohesion disproportionately important, and a small model may enter a different flow regime. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v15s-usbr-fish","v15s-usace-shields","v15s-usbr-redbluff","v15s-ebmud-freeport"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
